<% content_for :title, "Uptime Monitoring for Agencies | StatusPulse" %>
<% content_for :description, "Monitor every client from one dashboard, keep workspaces isolated, publish client status pages, and send SLA-ready uptime reports." %>

<aside class="mk-railstrip" aria-hidden="true" data-controller="rail">
  <span class="mk-railstrip__mark">
    <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
      <polyline points="22 12 18 12 15 21 9 3 6 12 2 12"></polyline>
    </svg>
  </span>
  <div class="mk-railstrip__bars" data-rail-target="bars"></div>
  <span class="mk-railstrip__label">Agency uptime</span>
</aside>

<div class="mk-shell">
<header class="mk-nav mk-wrap">
  <a href="<%= root_path %>" class="mk-nav__brand"><span class="mk-nav__mark"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="22 12 18 12 15 21 9 3 6 12 2 12"></polyline></svg></span><span class="mk-nav__word">StatusPulse</span></a>
  <nav class="mk-nav__links">
    <a href="<%= multi_tenant_uptime_monitoring_path %>">Workspaces</a>
    <a href="<%= client_uptime_reports_path %>">Reports</a>
    <a href="<%= org_public_status_path(org_slug: "statuspulse") %>">Demo status</a>
    <a href="<%= login_path %>" class="mk-nav__signin">Sign in</a>
    <a href="<%= signup_path %>" class="mk-btn mk-btn--sm">Create workspace</a>
  </nav>
</header>

<main>
  <section class="mk-hero mk-wrap">
    <div class="mk-hero__copy">
      <p class="mk-eyebrow">Uptime monitoring for agencies</p>
      <h1 class="mk-h1">Uptime monitoring for agencies.<br><span class="mk-h1__outline">Every client visible.</span></h1>
      <p class="mk-lede">StatusPulse gives agencies one console for client sites and APIs: isolated workspaces, real HTTP checks, public client status URLs, incident history, and SLA-ready reports.</p>
      <div class="mk-hero__actions">
        <a href="<%= signup_path %>" class="mk-btn">Create a workspace</a>
        <a href="<%= org_public_status_path(org_slug: "statuspulse") %>" class="mk-btn mk-btn--ghost">View status page demo</a>
      </div>
      <p class="mk-hero__note">Self-hostable. Runs on Postgres. No agent to install on client infrastructure.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mk-report" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="mk-report__head"><span class="mk-report__client">Client portfolio</span><span class="mk-report__range">Agency view</span></div>
      <div class="mk-report__tiles">
        <div class="mk-tile"><span class="mk-tile__label">Workspaces</span><span class="mk-tile__value">18</span></div>
        <div class="mk-tile"><span class="mk-tile__label">30d uptime</span><span class="mk-tile__value">99.91<i>%</i></span></div>
        <div class="mk-tile"><span class="mk-tile__label">P90 latency</span><span class="mk-tile__value">312<i>ms</i></span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-section mk-wrap">
    <div class="mk-section__head">
      <div class="mk-ticks" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
      <p class="mk-eyebrow">Agency problem</p>
      <h2 class="mk-h2">Generic uptime tools make client work messy.</h2>
      <p class="mk-body">One account per client creates login sprawl. One shared account blurs ownership. Raw monitor logs do not answer the question clients ask after an outage: what failed, when, and how long did it last?</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mk-grid mk-grid--3">
      <article class="mk-card"><h3 class="mk-h3">One workspace per client</h3><p class="mk-body">Endpoints, incidents, users, reports, and maintenance windows stay scoped to the organization they belong to.</p></article>
      <article class="mk-card"><h3 class="mk-h3">One console for the team</h3><p class="mk-body">Agency operators can watch many client workspaces without pretending every client is the same system.</p></article>
      <article class="mk-card"><h3 class="mk-h3">One public status URL</h3><p class="mk-body">Each workspace publishes to <code class="mk-code">/status/&lt;client&gt;</code>, so client stakeholders have a page to check during incidents.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-section mk-wrap">
    <div class="mk-section__head">
      <p class="mk-eyebrow">Workflow</p>
      <h2 class="mk-h2">Create a client workspace, add checks, publish status.</h2>
      <p class="mk-body">StatusPulse follows the way agencies already operate: configure the client once, monitor the real endpoints, then report uptime in language the client can read.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mk-grid mk-grid--3">
      <article class="mk-card"><h3 class="mk-h3">Real HTTP checks</h3><p class="mk-body">Use GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, HEAD, and OPTIONS with headers, request bodies, expected status codes, and response text assertions.</p></article>
      <article class="mk-card"><h3 class="mk-h3">Incident paper trail</h3><p class="mk-body">Record investigating, identified, monitoring, and resolved updates with timestamps and affected services.</p></article>
      <article class="mk-card"><h3 class="mk-h3">SLA-ready reporting</h3><p class="mk-body">Show 7, 30, and 90-day uptime, P90 latency, averages, and weekly digest summaries per workspace.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-cta mk-wrap">
    <h2 class="mk-h2">Start with one client. Add the rest.</h2>
    <p class="mk-body">Create the first workspace, point it at an endpoint, and publish a status URL when you are ready.</p>
    <a href="<%= signup_path %>" class="mk-btn mk-btn--lg">Create a workspace</a>
  </section>
</main>

<footer class="mk-footer mk-wrap">
  <span class="mk-footer__word">StatusPulse</span>
  <nav class="mk-footer__links">
    <a href="<%= root_path %>">Home</a>
    <a href="<%= multi_tenant_uptime_monitoring_path %>">Workspaces</a>
    <a href="<%= client_uptime_reports_path %>">Reports</a>
    <a href="<%= org_public_status_path(org_slug: "statuspulse") %>">Status</a>
    <a href="https://github.com/craigderington/statuspulse" rel="noopener">Source</a>
  </nav>
</footer>
</div>
